WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.434
-Our next guest can be seen
at the Dead Crow Comedy Room

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.901
in Wilmington,
North Carolina,

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:08.501
this Friday and Saturday.
Making her "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.834
please welcome the very funny
Sophie Buddle.

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:12.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:19.868
♪♪

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:22.601
-Hey. Hello.
Thank you so much.

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:25.467
Hi, everybody.
I'm really happy to be here.

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:28.634
I'm happy to be in the country.
I'm Canadian. I just --

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:29.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, Canadian?

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.501
Or you just love peace?

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.334
Fan of peacefulness.
That's cool.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.634
Yeah. I'm Canadian.
I moved to America this year.

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.567
I wanted to see it
before it ends.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:43.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.033
Just sort of a bucket list
thing for me.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:47.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.834
And I moved to L.A.

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:51.667
I moved to Los Angeles,
which is --

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:55.000
It's what you think it's like.
it's weird, right?

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.701
Like, the people there are
weird. I've never met people

00:00:57.701 --> 00:01:00.567
who actually say stuff out loud
in real life before.

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:03.200
Like, "Do you know
who my father is?"

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.501
And to be honest with you,
I do also say that,

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:08.567
but only because my dad

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.334
hasn't really opened up
to me like that.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:13.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:17.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:19.434
I'm just trying to see
if he talked to anybody else.

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:22.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.968
I will be honest with you.
This was not my dream.

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:28.734
No offense, Jim.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.501
You have a lovely home
and many root.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:34.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:38.000
So many root.
But this was not my dream.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.067
This is not what I wanted
for myself. When I was little,

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.367
I really was hoping that
I was going to become a spy.

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:45.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.300
It didn't work out for me.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.734
I stand on stage.

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:50.234
I tell secrets
into a microphone,

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:54.434
so it's not really what
they're looking for right now.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:56.133
But I remember
just being a little kid

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.901
and staying up late at night
and being like,

00:01:57.901 --> 00:02:00.801
"I hope when I grow up,
I'm hot enough to be a spy."

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.467
Because I just want to be
the best spy I could be.

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:06.267
And we all know from movies
and TV shows,

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:07.567
the best spies are hot.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.133
And they did a somersault
and they're wearing leather.

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:11.601
And you're like, "That's
impossible. That's amazing.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:15.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.234
Still got it.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.567
So I thought you had to be hot
to be a spy.

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:23.400
But I actually realized
as an adult woman,

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.100
you would make a much
more effective spy

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.367
if you're really frumpy-looking
because if you're all hot

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.467
and you're trying to break
into some big organization,

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:31.868
you're going to get there
and the security guard

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:34.534
is going to have
so many questions for you.

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:38.601
"How's it going?"
Like, grilling her.

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:40.734
But if you're all frumpy
and you show up and you're like,

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:43.367
"I have to do this paperwork,"
he's like, "Ew, fine. Go."

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:46.801
"Get in the vault. Hurry."

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:50.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.868
Nobody's more invisible
in our society than like

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:55.033
an average-looking woman.

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:58.367
And if that's offensive to you,
I can't see you.

00:02:58.367 --> 00:03:06.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:08.634
But I still do try
to make spy stuff

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:10.834
happen in my life as an adult.

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:13.501
Like, I go through
my boyfriend's phone.

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:15.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:17.467
And then I do a somersault. Wah!

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:19.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:22.868
But for real, the spy thing
that I think is really cool

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.234
that nobody really gives credit

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:27.400
to is the facial recognition
technology on our phones.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.033
It's awesome.
It's spy stuff, right?

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.367
You hold your phone
up to your face

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.901
and it scans your face
or something and that opens up

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:34.601
and you can just hold up
your boyfriend's phone

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.234
to his face
when he's sleeping, obviously.

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:39.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.267
You just hold it up.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.033
It feels like an oversight.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:48.100
Sometimes you do have to open up
their eyelids a little bit, but.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:53.234
It's like, "Oh, you're
dreaming."

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:54.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.367
"Go back to sleep."

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.033
But I do actually think

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:01.267
this facial recognition
technology is really cool,

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:02.934
but it has a really
bad reputation.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.033
Like, whenever you look into it,
everyone's always like,

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:07.033
"Ooh, you know the government's
actually using this

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:09.200
to look at us. Ooh, the
government's using that.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.100
Government's not going
to get my face."

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.601
And it's like it's always guys
that are freaking out

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:16.934
about the government
watching us and I don't care.

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:19.968
Girls don't care.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:23.667
And I think the reason that is,
is we're used to being looked at

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:25.734
when we don't want
to be looked at.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.000
That's just part
of our lives.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.434
But it's apparently
never happened to a man,

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:29.634
even one time, once.

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:31.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:33.834
They're freaking out.
The government's --

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:36.601
They're making a documentary.

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:38.200
They're writing a novel.
They can't believe it.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.868
"The government
is looking at me."

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:43.234
And so I think what
the government should do

00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:45.567
is I think the government
should like put out a statement

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:48.901
to these guys just being
like, "Smile, gorgeous."

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:52.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:58.567
[ Applause ]

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:01.467
"Take the compliment, babe."

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.334
Like, you know, when we get
all covered up in public

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:06.200
so nobody harasses us in public?
That's the same as when guys

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.834
put a little piece of tape
on their webcam.

00:05:09.834 --> 00:05:11.734
I just wish it was
that easy for us.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.901
If a guy's looking at you
and you feel uncomfortable,

00:05:13.901 --> 00:05:15.434
you should be allowed
to go up to him

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:18.000
and put a little bit
of tape on his eyes.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.234
Okay, I'm Sophie Buddle.
Thank you so much.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:23.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.434
-Oh, my goodness.
Thank you so much.

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:28.300
Sophie Buddle!

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:30.968
See Sophie this Friday

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.167
and Saturday
at the Dead Crow Comedy Room

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:35.300
in Wilmington,
North Carolina.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:36.801
We'll be right back,
everybody.

